{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.meteorology",
    "description": "Template library: the whole arithmetic of `MeteorologyGenerator.doHeatIndex` -- the one MOVES pass that WRITES `ZoneMonthHour.heatIndex`, `ZoneMonthHour.specificHumidity` and `ZoneMonthHour.molWaterFraction`. Ports crates/moves-calculators/src/generators/meteorology.rs, which ports gov/epa/otaq/moves/master/implementation/general/MeteorologyGenerator.java. Specified in docs/meteorology-generator.md.\n\nWHY A LIBRARY RATHER THAN A CALCULATOR'S OWN FILE. Nine fixtures in this repository INGEST those three columns -- process-pm-exhaust, process-tirewear, process-brakewear, process-crankcase-running, process-refueling, process-airtoxics, process-nox-speciation, mixed-onroad and nr-logging-county each name at least one of the three in a `float_columns` list, three of them (nr-logging-county, process-crankcase-running, process-nox-speciation) naming all three and the other six naming `heatIndex` alone -- and until docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.2 nothing here produced any of them. They now do: eight of the nine COMPUTE their heat index from `temperature` and `relHumidity` through `heat_index`, two of those eight also compute both humidity columns, and nr-logging-county reads none of the three (its NONROAD snapshot leaves all three NULL). What each fixture's retarget did and did not move is docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.2's table. They are inputs to `lib/adjustments.esm`'s `nox_humidity_cfr86` (specific humidity) and `nox_humidity_cfr1065` (water mole fraction) and to every heat-index-gated air-conditioning branch. One generator step, so by docs/esm-conventions.md 1 it is one place; a template library rather than a component because the arithmetic is per ROW and carries no axis of its own, exactly as lib/adjustments.esm's factors do.\n\nTHE CHAIN, IN THE ORDER THE JAVA THREADS IT THROUGH TEMPORARY TABLES. `TK` is `fahrenheit_to_kelvin`; `PH2O` is `saturation_vapor_pressure`; `PV` is `vapor_partial_pressure`; `XH2O` is `mol_water_fraction` and is written straight to `molWaterFraction`; `specificHumidity` is `specific_humidity`. `heat_index` is a separate two-statement UPDATE that does not join the pressure chain at all, which is why it takes no pressure.\n\nTHE CONVERSION FACTOR IS THE EXACT 5/9, AND THAT IS MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. The Java writes the Fahrenheit-to-Kelvin slope as the SQL literal `(5/9)`, and moves.rs's port records an open question about it: in MariaDB `5/9` is DECIMAL division, rounded to `div_precision_increment` places, which would make the slope 0.5556 rather than 0.5555555555555556. The two are not interchangeable here. Reproduced against the snapshot corpus both ways, the exact ratio lands the corpus's 532 populated `ZoneMonthHour` rows -- 1,596 cells -- at a worst 2.391e-08 relative, and 0.5556 lands the same cells at a worst 1.379e-04: four orders worse, and seven times `tolerance.toml`'s 2e-5 per-cell gate. MOVES computes with the exact ratio. It is written here as a `/` of two literals rather than as 0.5555555555555556 so that the SQL it came from is still legible; docs/meteorology-generator.md 7.2 has the measurement.\n\n`power_of_ten` exists because the exponent form uses it five times -- three times inside the Goff-Gratch exponent (twice as `10^-4` / `10^-3` coefficient scalings the SQL writes as `power(10,-4)` and `power(10,-3)`, once as the inner `10^(-8.2969*(x-1))`), once more as the other inner decade, and once to raise 10 to the finished exponent. Writing `1.50475e-4` instead would be the same number and would lose the SQL's own shape; writing `10^x` five times over would be docs/esm-conventions.md 6's repetition.\n\n`ice_point_over_temperature` and `temperature_over_ice_point` are the Goff-Gratch reduced temperature and its reciprocal. They are TWO templates and not one plus a `1/`, because the SQL writes `TK/273.15` and `273.15/TK` as separate expressions and the two spellings do not round alike; the same reason moves.rs's port gives for keeping them apart. Between them they are applied five times inside one exponent.\n\n`vapor_partial_pressure_from_weather` is `fahrenheit_to_kelvin` -> `saturation_vapor_pressure` -> `vapor_partial_pressure` composed BY REFERENCE, and it exists because of who consumes it. Two fixtures (process-crankcase-running, process-nox-speciation) need `PV` and need it only as a step towards the two humidity columns; without this template each would have to thread `TK` and `PH2O` as named variables of its own, and the ORDER of the three steps -- which is the only thing those three variables encode -- would be written down in three documents instead of one. It carries no arithmetic: every formula in it still lives in exactly one of the three templates it applies. components/meteorology.esm applies it too, and keeps `met_temperatureKelvin` and `met_saturationVaporPressure` as separately computed PROBES because its tests pin each intermediate against MOVES; recomputing two expressions over 24 rows costs nothing and is the price of having the order in one place.\n\n`ambient_pressure_kilopascals` is the `barometricPressure * 3.38639` that BOTH humidity outputs divide by. One template, so that a document cannot convert the pressure one way for the mole fraction and another way for the specific humidity -- the divergence that would be invisible in either output alone because each is separately plausible.\n\nTHE COUNTY DEFAULT FILL is `resolved_barometric_pressure` and `resolved_altitude_is_high`, the two `UPDATE County` statements the generator runs BEFORE the humidity pass, in that order. The order is load-bearing: step 1 fills a missing pressure from the altitude CLASS, and step 2 then classes a missing altitude from the pressure step 1 has just written -- so a county missing both gets 28.94 inHg from step 1's `ELSE` branch and is classed Low by step 2, never High. `pressure_is_present` and `altitude_is_known` are the SQL's `IS NULL` guards carried as indicators, because a `.esm` parameter that failed to ingest arrives as its `default` rather than as a null and the two cases have to be told apart by a column rather than by a value. NOTE, and docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.1 says it again: not one of the 22,815 `County` rows across the corpus's 40 snapshots has a missing or non-positive `barometricPressure`, and every one records an altitude of `H` or `L`, so these two templates' fallback arms are ported from the SQL and are NOT checked against MOVES anywhere in this repository.\n\nThe 24.59 in `default_pressure_high_altitude` is the value the executed SQL carries; MeteorologyGenerator.java's own `@algorithm` comment says 24.69, and moves.rs follows the executed literal. Neither is exercised by the corpus, so this file follows the code MOVES runs and says so rather than choosing quietly.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "onroad", "meteorology", "generator", "template-library"]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "inches_hg_to_kilopascals": { "params": [], "body": 3.38639 },
    "water_ice_point_kelvin": { "params": [], "body": 273.15 },
    "fahrenheit_freezing_point": { "params": [], "body": 32.0 },
    "percent_scale": { "params": [], "body": 100.0 },
    "heat_index_threshold": { "params": [], "body": 78.0 },
    "heat_index_ceiling": { "params": [], "body": 120.0 },
    "specific_humidity_constant": { "params": [], "body": 621.1 },
    "default_pressure_high_altitude": { "params": [], "body": 24.59 },
    "default_pressure_low_altitude": { "params": [], "body": 28.94 },
    "altitude_pressure_threshold": { "params": [], "body": 25.8403 },

    "power_of_ten": {
      "params": ["exponent"],
      "body": { "op": "^", "args": [10.0, "exponent"] }
    },

    "fahrenheit_to_kelvin": {
      "params": ["temperature_degF"],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            { "op": "/", "args": [5.0, 9.0] },
            { "op": "-", "args": ["temperature_degF",
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "fahrenheit_freezing_point", "bindings": {} }] }] },
          { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "water_ice_point_kelvin", "bindings": {} }
        ]
      }
    },

    "temperature_over_ice_point": {
      "params": ["temperature_kelvin"],
      "body": { "op": "/", "args": ["temperature_kelvin",
        { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "water_ice_point_kelvin", "bindings": {} }] }
    },

    "ice_point_over_temperature": {
      "params": ["temperature_kelvin"],
      "body": { "op": "/", "args": [
        { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "water_ice_point_kelvin", "bindings": {} },
        "temperature_kelvin"] }
    },

    "saturation_vapor_pressure_exponent": {
      "params": ["temperature_kelvin"],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          { "op": "*", "args": [10.79574,
            { "op": "-", "args": [1.0,
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "ice_point_over_temperature",
                "bindings": { "temperature_kelvin": "temperature_kelvin" } }] }] },
          { "op": "*", "args": [-5.028,
            { "op": "log10", "args": [
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "temperature_over_ice_point",
                "bindings": { "temperature_kelvin": "temperature_kelvin" } }] }] },
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            { "op": "*", "args": [1.50475,
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "power_of_ten", "bindings": { "exponent": -4.0 } }] },
            { "op": "-", "args": [1.0,
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "power_of_ten", "bindings": {
                "exponent": { "op": "*", "args": [-8.2969,
                  { "op": "-", "args": [
                    { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "temperature_over_ice_point",
                      "bindings": { "temperature_kelvin": "temperature_kelvin" } },
                    1.0] }] } } }] }] },
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            { "op": "*", "args": [0.42873,
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "power_of_ten", "bindings": { "exponent": -3.0 } }] },
            { "op": "-", "args": [
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "power_of_ten", "bindings": {
                "exponent": { "op": "*", "args": [4.76955,
                  { "op": "-", "args": [1.0,
                    { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "ice_point_over_temperature",
                      "bindings": { "temperature_kelvin": "temperature_kelvin" } }] }] } } },
              1.0] }] },
          -0.2138602
        ]
      }
    },

    "saturation_vapor_pressure": {
      "params": ["temperature_kelvin"],
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "power_of_ten",
        "bindings": {
          "exponent": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "saturation_vapor_pressure_exponent",
            "bindings": { "temperature_kelvin": "temperature_kelvin" }
          }
        }
      }
    },

    "vapor_partial_pressure": {
      "params": ["rel_humidity_percent", "saturation_pressure_kpa"],
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          { "op": "/", "args": ["rel_humidity_percent",
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "percent_scale", "bindings": {} }] },
          "saturation_pressure_kpa"
        ]
      }
    },

    "vapor_partial_pressure_from_weather": {
      "params": ["temperature_degF", "rel_humidity_percent"],
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "vapor_partial_pressure",
        "bindings": {
          "rel_humidity_percent": "rel_humidity_percent",
          "saturation_pressure_kpa": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "saturation_vapor_pressure",
            "bindings": {
              "temperature_kelvin": {
                "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "fahrenheit_to_kelvin",
                "bindings": { "temperature_degF": "temperature_degF" }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },

    "ambient_pressure_kilopascals": {
      "params": ["barometric_pressure_inhg"],
      "body": { "op": "*", "args": ["barometric_pressure_inhg",
        { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "inches_hg_to_kilopascals", "bindings": {} }] }
    },

    "mol_water_fraction": {
      "params": ["vapor_pressure_kpa", "barometric_pressure_inhg"],
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": ["vapor_pressure_kpa",
          { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "ambient_pressure_kilopascals",
            "bindings": { "barometric_pressure_inhg": "barometric_pressure_inhg" } }]
      }
    },

    "specific_humidity": {
      "params": ["vapor_pressure_kpa", "barometric_pressure_inhg"],
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "specific_humidity_constant", "bindings": {} },
            "vapor_pressure_kpa"] },
          { "op": "-", "args": [
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "ambient_pressure_kilopascals",
              "bindings": { "barometric_pressure_inhg": "barometric_pressure_inhg" } },
            "vapor_pressure_kpa"] }
        ]
      }
    },

    "heat_index_regression": {
      "params": ["temperature_degF", "rel_humidity_percent"],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          -42.379,
          { "op": "*", "args": [2.04901523, "temperature_degF"] },
          { "op": "*", "args": [10.14333127, "rel_humidity_percent"] },
          { "op": "*", "args": [-0.22475541, "temperature_degF", "rel_humidity_percent"] },
          { "op": "*", "args": [-0.00683783, "temperature_degF", "temperature_degF"] },
          { "op": "*", "args": [-0.05481717, "rel_humidity_percent", "rel_humidity_percent"] },
          { "op": "*", "args": [0.00122874, "temperature_degF", "temperature_degF", "rel_humidity_percent"] },
          { "op": "*", "args": [0.00085282, "temperature_degF", "rel_humidity_percent", "rel_humidity_percent"] },
          { "op": "*", "args": [-0.00000199, "temperature_degF", "temperature_degF",
            "rel_humidity_percent", "rel_humidity_percent"] }
        ]
      }
    },

    "heat_index": {
      "params": ["temperature_degF", "rel_humidity_percent"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": "<", "args": ["temperature_degF",
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "heat_index_threshold", "bindings": {} }] },
          "temperature_degF",
          { "op": "min", "args": [
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "heat_index_regression",
              "bindings": { "temperature_degF": "temperature_degF",
                            "rel_humidity_percent": "rel_humidity_percent" } },
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "heat_index_ceiling", "bindings": {} }] }
        ]
      }
    },

    "resolved_barometric_pressure": {
      "params": ["barometric_pressure_inhg", "pressure_is_present", "altitude_is_high"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": "and", "args": [
            { "op": ">", "args": ["pressure_is_present", 0.0] },
            { "op": ">", "args": ["barometric_pressure_inhg", 0.0] }] },
          "barometric_pressure_inhg",
          { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
            { "op": ">", "args": ["altitude_is_high", 0.0] },
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "default_pressure_high_altitude", "bindings": {} },
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "default_pressure_low_altitude", "bindings": {} }] }
        ]
      }
    },

    "resolved_altitude_is_high": {
      "params": ["altitude_is_known", "altitude_is_high", "resolved_pressure_inhg"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": ">", "args": ["altitude_is_known", 0.0] },
          "altitude_is_high",
          { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
            { "op": "<", "args": ["resolved_pressure_inhg",
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "altitude_pressure_threshold", "bindings": {} }] },
            1.0,
            0.0] }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
